          "short": "$1500\\times0.1=1500\\times\\frac{1}{10}=1500\\div10=150$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}1500\\times0.1&=1500\\times\\frac{1}{10}\\\\1500\\times0.1&=1500\\div10\\\\1500\\times0.1&=150\\end{align*}$$ Since $0.1=\\frac{1}{10}$, multiplying any number by $0.1$ is the same as dividing it by $10$.",
